---
description: Rules for HTML structure and CSS styling to prevent token bloat
globs: *.html, *.css, css/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

# HTML & CSS Standards
- Use semantic HTML5 elements (`<header>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`).
- Design mobile-first using CSS Flexbox and Grid.
- Use native CSS custom properties (variables) for colors, fonts, and spacing.
- Never write inline styles or embed `<style>` tags directly inside HTML.

# Token-Saving Instructions
- Do not rewrite the entire HTML file for minor edits; output only the specific modified block or element.
- Keep comments minimal: write self-documenting class names (BEM style preferred if requested).
- Do not inject external frameworks (like Tailwind or Bootstrap) unless explicitly told.
